x$ and $y$ area measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of this lamina about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})(6-xy)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}6{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}y+6{y}^{2}-x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[2{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}y+6x{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}16-4y+12{y}^{2}-2{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[16y-2{y}^{2}+4{y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{4}]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =48-18+108-\\frac{81}{2}-0 \\\\  & =97.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia of the lamina about the origin is $97.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-162922/selection/ma-v1/d69bf1a5086d9f9d2ed263a2b89a574264e6fd5bdca2d23bd14d5c5443d69ce4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-163146/selection/b787f7ea701d7e390a3b4790af391cf7249ba5845760d6131ed8e1d2d292aa45" :answer/id #uuid "91f9b625-df19-5f5e-a030-ee60b051098e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163146/selection/0cd12da4b8620205de4e895a46f82ea983a7f0c821433c9c686c1fa5cc1ee8e0" :answer/id #uuid "66686c14-240c-5499-994c-2e573bd1e5db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163146/selection/0e61b8d4ba66f20a5dc6b1c298b77aef2b3c7eee11ea9f6b5812b65630264f39" :answer/id #uuid "59e83f3b-c47f-5e82-87f4-ba33cf0a2b66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163146/selection/a162f140b57b3f5ada92102fa3de2598b37afe3f34d7dff7707aa185fd284397" :answer/id #uuid "8037ba45-c4ae-5f45-9a1f-0cc83372148b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163146/selection/4cd78daa345563b28464689074b1f86265cdfa041e2f2373b41faf2a807390fb" :answer/id #uuid "d04c5e36-7464-5e87-89a2-8006f03b7e00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163146/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bc0c365a-dbfe-57ac-a777-1d559f1db0e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163146/selection/b787f7ea701d7e390a3b4790af391cf7249ba5845760d6131ed8e1d2d292aa45" :answer-field/choices ["q-163146/selection/b787f7ea701d7e390a3b4790af391cf7249ba5845760d6131ed8e1d2d292aa45" "q-163146/selection/0cd12da4b8620205de4e895a46f82ea983a7f0c821433c9c686c1fa5cc1ee8e0" "q-163146/selection/0e61b8d4ba66f20a5dc6b1c298b77aef2b3c7eee11ea9f6b5812b65630264f39" "q-163146/selection/a162f140b57b3f5ada92102fa3de2598b37afe3f34d7dff7707aa185fd284397" "q-163146/selection/4cd78daa345563b28464689074b1f86265cdfa041e2f2373b41faf2a807390fb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163146" :question/id #uuid "567c1d0c-a247-52c4-bf76-77c7361081f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-163146" :question/problem "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}$\nwith mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=(x+y)\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},$ where $x$ and $y$ area measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of this lamina about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}y]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4+\\frac{8y}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[4y+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =12+12 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $y$-axis is $24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163146/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fdc1a2a-8a35-59f2-9890-5b835693df4f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163146"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163219/selection/b85071a9e8b7d547fca77b2b77bca7f235cba5e00a1a199e5312d710423f08c1" :answer/id #uuid "6d2b9ca3-bc1a-5ff9-adc7-fce2197d707a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163219/selection/c9067cd5c3287f49d8f514bcc0bd81695dfcd0cbc258703db0652d842d2af6a7" :answer/id #uuid "b32ba64b-9d31-5c48-b895-5c66576bad5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{M}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163219/selection/c1cf1741ff3ce28c22251c4f3e2762a87f7716494a4c9965082e43b49bc9e431" :answer/id #uuid "da917780-39cd-5928-9fdc-5504eb35b69b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163219/selection/2c5155831b5a23d32841a0bf3ddd187afd25a845d2bd2496cae1e88e123db299" :answer/id #uuid "190d8080-e400-57a6-b5b8-8afabda13574" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3M}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163219/selection/b46df820bdeb989272f0bbb9084137cf2443a692578378dfe29e41bb10710705" :answer/id #uuid "b73bdc1f-af7c-5714-bddb-c368e2f4687a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2M}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163219/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e76fa7e-92b9-5529-9a53-a0882995a30b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163219/selection/b46df820bdeb989272f0bbb9084137cf2443a692578378dfe29e41bb10710705" :answer-field/choices ["q-163219/selection/b85071a9e8b7d547fca77b2b77bca7f235cba5e00a1a199e5312d710423f08c1" "q-163219/selection/c9067cd5c3287f49d8f514bcc0bd81695dfcd0cbc258703db0652d842d2af6a7" "q-163219/selection/c1cf1741ff3ce28c22251c4f3e2762a87f7716494a4c9965082e43b49bc9e431" "q-163219/selection/2c5155831b5a23d32841a0bf3ddd187afd25a845d2bd2496cae1e88e123db299" "q-163219/selection/b46df820bdeb989272f0bbb9084137cf2443a692578378dfe29e41bb10710705"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163219" :question/id #uuid "241848f8-5ad9-56aa-808b-8b4d0f7ad9b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-163219" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/c683f411b11b7b353e166364c8e0fdbc0d218c07535c2f3430d832ab129702d8.png)\n\nA triangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the $y$-axis and the lines $y=\\frac{x}{2}$ and $y=3-x,$ as shown above. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,\\frac{x}{2}\\le y\\le 3-x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/6c2cec5e919c25623396b5ba5f052481623a868c7520aa8e3d1d3eb34f3a4a58.png)\n\nThe area of the triangular plate $D$ is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 3=3.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, every unit of area contains the same amount of mass. Therefore, the mass density is constant and is given by the total mass divided by the total area:\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x/2}^{3-x}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{x/2}^{3-x}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}(3-x-\\frac{x}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{[{x}^{3}-\\frac{3}{8}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}(8-6) \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163219/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92cc3d27-0e31-571f-9b92-4f209c5a08e0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163219"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186129466 :question/answer-fields 17592186126602] {:db/id "q-162905/selection/ma-v1/711899b6c37344fc1f553420bdb5621cbadae37b2b7d4353030efe2acd4b9850/a47bb74a2831c0aa139acc4e1f2ecb8045e1f93f48e8d5cc304b471eb5d0e2a1" :answer/id #uuid "b3428d5f-9137-5d72-a1e6-aede2246c334" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162905/selection/ma-v1/711899b6c37344fc1f553420bdb5621cbadae37b2b7d4353030efe2acd4b9850/80edf33584a259eaa31e922d34f0e1a0e0a4269890cb31da1468b18e2a0c0a88" :answer/id #uuid "fd81b4e7-ffb1-58eb-a458-95b4181c57bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162905/selection/ma-v1/711899b6c37344fc1f553420bdb5621cbadae37b2b7d4353030efe2acd4b9850/969e7eb5ea8a7c7c27a004b99580270eee8a08615bef2d34c86b0ae06ad319eb" :answer/id #uuid "7fc56543-759b-54d0-a7fd-5e7d8021187a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162905/selection/ma-v1/711899b6c37344fc1f553420bdb5621cbadae37b2b7d4353030efe2acd4b9850/62190863b48120b313831aa6a3568baa4ea9d73536705784d93f44abcf46f56d" :answer/id #uuid "92171c15-efca-5856-a07d-979bbc4af5e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162905/selection/ma-v1/711899b6c37344fc1f553420bdb5621cbadae37b2b7d4353030efe2acd4b9850/42e551056e1ffdcd5a017a993dc8222b601079cdd6d84277b2bbf9a0751b3d51" :answer/id #uuid "63d942ae-7ca7-5f90-8642-65c757b1b8a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162905/selection/ma-v1/711899b6c37344fc1f553420bdb5621cbadae37b2b7d4353030efe2acd4b9850" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c9e89ea-a32a-5f42-b5df-2f12d0b16131" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162905/selection/ma-v1/711899b6c37344fc1f553420bdb5621cbadae37b2b7d4353030efe2acd4b9850/62190863b48120b313831aa6a3568baa4ea9d73536705784d93f44abcf46f56d" :answer-field/choices ["q-162905/selection/ma-v1/711899b6c37344fc1f553420bdb5621cbadae37b2b7d4353030efe2acd4b9850/a47bb74a2831c0aa139acc4e1f2ecb8045e1f93f48e8d5cc304b471eb5d0e2a1" "q-162905/selection/ma-v1/711899b6c37344fc1f553420bdb5621cbadae37b2b7d4353030efe2acd4b9850/80edf33584a259eaa31e922d34f0e1a0e0a4269890cb31da1468b18e2a0c0a88" "q-162905/selection/ma-v1/711899b6c37344fc1f553420bdb5621cbadae37b2b7d4353030efe2acd4b9850/969e7eb5ea8a7c7c27a004b99580270eee8a08615bef2d34c86b0ae06ad319eb" "q-162905/selection/ma-v1/711899b6c37344fc1f553420bdb5621cbadae37b2b7d4353030efe2acd4b9850/62190863b48120b313831aa6a3568baa4ea9d73536705784d93f44abcf46f56d" "q-162905/selection/ma-v1/711899b6c37344fc1f553420bdb5621cbadae37b2b7d4353030efe2acd4b9850/42e551056e1ffdcd5a017a993dc8222b601079cdd6d84277b2bbf9a0751b3d51"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-162905"] :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2},$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 2=2.$ \n\nSince the plate has uniform density, every unit of area contains the same amount of mass. Therefore, the mass density is constant and is given by the total mass divided by the total area:\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{10}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $\\frac{5M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-162905/selection/ma-v1/711899b6c37344fc1f553420bdb5621cbadae37b2b7d4353030efe2acd4b9850"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-163200/selection/c87e0a9f7e24df094c367dcbdb2af72bd4c9d923de26a91cefec8759dcf57a9c" :answer/id #uuid "ac2fa324-8b6c-5fce-af77-b1abb4b29b7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8M}{9}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163200/selection/5bf409329eaf0a5ab45855294a9665a8791165efd8faf5e84f3211fb0e42b6e1" :answer/id #uuid "2cdda060-9202-592a-92bf-841692f3c5d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163200/selection/6bb1af76465dddabdf295cbaf0cf76d376389e9ee4689049bebf0a83b6ab39ca" :answer/id #uuid "c22ca50d-9e77-58a5-9164-d2bd4133b2ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163200/selection/0ef28886baa91121491d2619f961b932d210004d66706a88127803a64c1dac85" :answer/id #uuid "7ee795c3-412f-5107-9cb9-1762c7cb3946" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163200/selection/3841c95a1f818ad226d28e2b41250c937addb7b50e3342cc8d438295de5883d3" :answer/id #uuid "726114c7-bbe3-5a44-81ca-b02d8db567a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163200/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2a61c7d5-8b5c-5b7f-a488-5712f640356b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163200/selection/6bb1af76465dddabdf295cbaf0cf76d376389e9ee4689049bebf0a83b6ab39ca" :answer-field/choices ["q-163200/selection/c87e0a9f7e24df094c367dcbdb2af72bd4c9d923de26a91cefec8759dcf57a9c" "q-163200/selection/5bf409329eaf0a5ab45855294a9665a8791165efd8faf5e84f3211fb0e42b6e1" "q-163200/selection/6bb1af76465dddabdf295cbaf0cf76d376389e9ee4689049bebf0a83b6ab39ca" "q-163200/selection/0ef28886baa91121491d2619f961b932d210004d66706a88127803a64c1dac85" "q-163200/selection/3841c95a1f818ad226d28e2b41250c937addb7b50e3342cc8d438295de5883d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163200" :question/id #uuid "bdbe5d34-53d8-5fa8-ab86-b773c4a96924" :question/math-academy-id "q-163200" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 4},$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 3=9.$ \n\nSince the plate has uniform density, every unit of area contains the same amount of mass. Therefore, the mass density is constant and is given by the total mass divided by the total area:\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{9}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{1}^{4}9+3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{[9y+{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}(36+64-9-1) \\\\  & =10M\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $10M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163200/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92cc3d27-0e31-571f-9b92-4f209c5a08e0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163200"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163204/selection/6271c4f60e64535f70cfdb4ba6671fd9fbb0577afefa804ab37afa9d35fa794b" :answer/id #uuid "70123a16-b5fa-58d6-b8ba-b239f81826f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163204/selection/969e7eb5ea8a7c7c27a004b99580270eee8a08615bef2d34c86b0ae06ad319eb" :answer/id #uuid "d75264c0-fda0-5330-b7a1-f956fd948186" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163204/selection/a47bb74a2831c0aa139acc4e1f2ecb8045e1f93f48e8d5cc304b471eb5d0e2a1" :answer/id #uuid "1ad647f5-560d-5d2d-b6db-c8030bd75321" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163204/selection/8c198dd43dbe1c58278693aab386553a1328a9b3b6717bc3144373143dfad582" :answer/id #uuid "41efbba0-2e82-554e-985c-edd9c3305f7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163204/selection/13fb638d02f3a43d78cae389f7b80c73b37394bb65a4777eaf086e2e286281f2" :answer/id #uuid "015aa5d4-82bd-5776-aee9-772d09b74aa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163204/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c67bffe3-ab54-5774-84cd-532a1173c729" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163204/selection/a47bb74a2831c0aa139acc4e1f2ecb8045e1f93f48e8d5cc304b471eb5d0e2a1" :answer-field/choices ["q-163204/selection/6271c4f60e64535f70cfdb4ba6671fd9fbb0577afefa804ab37afa9d35fa794b" "q-163204/selection/969e7eb5ea8a7c7c27a004b99580270eee8a08615bef2d34c86b0ae06ad319eb" "q-163204/selection/a47bb74a2831c0aa139acc4e1f2ecb8045e1f93f48e8d5cc304b471eb5d0e2a1" "q-163204/selection/8c198dd43dbe1c58278693aab386553a1328a9b3b6717bc3144373143dfad582" "q-163204/selection/13fb638d02f3a43d78cae389f7b80c73b37394bb65a4777eaf086e2e286281f2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163204" :question/id #uuid "79ad7a44-69b7-56af-9f4d-f253dc7ebf95" :question/math-academy-id "q-163204" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3},$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 2=4.$ \n\nSince the plate has uniform density, every unit of area contains the same amount of mass. Therefore, the mass density is constant and is given by the total mass divided by the total area:\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{4}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{8}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{[\\frac{8y}{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{3}(3-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $\\frac{4M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163204/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92cc3d27-0e31-571f-9b92-4f209c5a08e0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163204"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163217/selection/167d2b11bf44b832a9ba8dc741d9cf2f1505f937a4dd5e96fc9d1759f78b6852" :answer/id #uuid "cbb20b5a-b47c-5eb6-81c2-91d3970ea90c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{M}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163217/selection/b85071a9e8b7d547fca77b2b77bca7f235cba5e00a1a199e5312d710423f08c1" :answer/id #uuid "f47f5895-e52d-5cb1-a5a4-2aae43678d8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163217/selection/c9067cd5c3287f49d8f514bcc0bd81695dfcd0cbc258703db0652d842d2af6a7" :answer/id #uuid "aa3544b6-e032-526f-a164-ef74ea80aabf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{M}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163217/selection/a76e3ee4f865d6c2a9df0bd48d492bbb24f18ca0b45f19f823c1a6f6f867a586" :answer/id #uuid "413ef5e7-06b3-55df-a5f0-694083b4c0f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3M}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163217/selection/c1cf1741ff3ce28c22251c4f3e2762a87f7716494a4c9965082e43b49bc9e431" :answer/id #uuid "d3df9fb8-d934-55c9-bb4b-7236aaa66940" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163217/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d7449fa-6802-5070-99f2-2c2cd1437003" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163217/selection/a76e3ee4f865d6c2a9df0bd48d492bbb24f18ca0b45f19f823c1a6f6f867a586" :answer-field/choices ["q-163217/selection/167d2b11bf44b832a9ba8dc741d9cf2f1505f937a4dd5e96fc9d1759f78b6852" "q-163217/selection/b85071a9e8b7d547fca77b2b77bca7f235cba5e00a1a199e5312d710423f08c1" "q-163217/selection/c9067cd5c3287f49d8f514bcc0bd81695dfcd0cbc258703db0652d842d2af6a7" "q-163217/selection/a76e3ee4f865d6c2a9df0bd48d492bbb24f18ca0b45f19f823c1a6f6f867a586" "q-163217/selection/c1cf1741ff3ce28c22251c4f3e2762a87f7716494a4c9965082e43b49bc9e431"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163217" :question/id #uuid "79941e95-b786-504a-89df-1f073b7dd438" :question/math-academy-id "q-163217" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/de3753a45554be28283e74116510ff6c3b67560fce79d1570c819a215f6e10f3.png)\n\nA triangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the $x$-axis and the lines $y=3x$ and $y=4-x,$ as shown above. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type II region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,\\frac{y}{3}\\le x\\le 4-y},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/47c897bd58a23965d9c36f683553c0817afa8bc2e37ed53a432edcd62b386e55.png)\n\nThe area of the triangular plate $D$ is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, every unit of area contains the same amount of mass. Therefore, the mass density is constant and is given by the total mass divided by the total area:\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{y/3}^{4-y}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{y/3}^{4-y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}(4-y-\\frac{1}{3}y)\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{y}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{[\\frac{4}{3}{y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{4}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(36-27) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163217/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92cc3d27-0e31-571f-9b92-4f209c5a08e0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163217"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163180/selection/2d5cc1b82e4d2397aebab16900d6ac54fc2f42957cd22a51396b7f52816d146b" :answer/id #uuid "5a0b84bc-628a-5173-906c-44830a8aee5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163180/selection/c9067cd5c3287f49d8f514bcc0bd81695dfcd0cbc258703db0652d842d2af6a7" :answer/id #uuid "73c1e694-e7d4-5518-ab83-8afc20afe7d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{M}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163180/selection/167d2b11bf44b832a9ba8dc741d9cf2f1505f937a4dd5e96fc9d1759f78b6852" :answer/id #uuid "d6aa7e02-f624-574e-bb4e-88134b2affc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{M}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163180/selection/c1cf1741ff3ce28c22251c4f3e2762a87f7716494a4c9965082e43b49bc9e431" :answer/id #uuid "3e4fd8ae-55f7-50aa-932b-003440a00ce7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163180/selection/b85071a9e8b7d547fca77b2b77bca7f235cba5e00a1a199e5312d710423f08c1" :answer/id #uuid "0b399939-864d-5411-99c0-09e69ee0ac82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163180/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb2c7b68-a5b3-5920-aa62-d8a781ac907a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163180/selection/b85071a9e8b7d547fca77b2b77bca7f235cba5e00a1a199e5312d710423f08c1" :answer-field/choices ["q-163180/selection/2d5cc1b82e4d2397aebab16900d6ac54fc2f42957cd22a51396b7f52816d146b" "q-163180/selection/c9067cd5c3287f49d8f514bcc0bd81695dfcd0cbc258703db0652d842d2af6a7" "q-163180/selection/167d2b11bf44b832a9ba8dc741d9cf2f1505f937a4dd5e96fc9d1759f78b6852" "q-163180/selection/c1cf1741ff3ce28c22251c4f3e2762a87f7716494a4c9965082e43b49bc9e431" "q-163180/selection/b85071a9e8b7d547fca77b2b77bca7f235cba5e00a1a199e5312d710423f08c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163180" :question/id #uuid "a8bb967c-3713-5f4d-a731-98f880cc76f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-163180" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $x$-axis.\nFind the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFrom the description, the mass density function can be written as\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k|y|=ky,\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find an expression for $k$ in terms of $M$ by integrating the density function over the plate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}ky\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =k[x]_{0}^{3}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =k(3-0)(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3k}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\frac{2M}{3}$ and hence,\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=ky=\\frac{2M}{3}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{3}({\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{3}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{3}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{3}(9-0)(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =3M.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163180/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89f280af-9947-5d54-9284-9ae75d46c682"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163180"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163186/selection/55177d86b4e8030fbeda5238fe712f3cf39aeb2d2e53ad8c5faaa071c564b26f" :answer/id #uuid "7b915a04-7d07-5279-a976-5d8ed6f3a5dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{M}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163186/selection/33aa5cf2a65c7eb1b5df58f39dc560db17b01239ef2ebdc004910577cb52b672" :answer/id #uuid "248aa271-9fed-56db-aa8f-33e3edd221ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5M}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163186/selection/c70bd73d09f6c832745b538ce96c359ab9c75cc4cabee07d243dbdadaa1aceb2" :answer/id #uuid "1ec3ff84-9b57-52f9-83f2-5b24743886d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2M}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163186/selection/cdc193883a54b165424031a8ef51d0ee3f14dfb753e2946ca88e04743753f2f2" :answer/id #uuid "16083e51-11b0-5a19-982b-a26975d3c199" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7M}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163186/selection/5ba3a63e0f0ce5e2e83e130cf881fb987cc5452413a1e2b100c279eaa5e96270" :answer/id #uuid "f66ff212-5369-5e1e-b590-da1a09692154" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4M}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163186/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "70b3f9a6-e0ce-518d-a889-3f10144e1a0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163186/selection/c70bd73d09f6c832745b538ce96c359ab9c75cc4cabee07d243dbdadaa1aceb2" :answer-field/choices ["q-163186/selection/55177d86b4e8030fbeda5238fe712f3cf39aeb2d2e53ad8c5faaa071c564b26f" "q-163186/selection/33aa5cf2a65c7eb1b5df58f39dc560db17b01239ef2ebdc004910577cb52b672" "q-163186/selection/c70bd73d09f6c832745b538ce96c359ab9c75cc4cabee07d243dbdadaa1aceb2" "q-163186/selection/cdc193883a54b165424031a8ef51d0ee3f14dfb753e2946ca88e04743753f2f2" "q-163186/selection/5ba3a63e0f0ce5e2e83e130cf881fb987cc5452413a1e2b100c279eaa5e96270"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163186" :question/id #uuid "62c73ee4-534d-5429-b48c-9e2202076205" :question/math-academy-id "q-163186" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/043119a0637985fa55a7084a8d4b67df5031b24211ab421ec019700235ca2365.png)\n\nA triangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant enclosed by the line $y=1-x$ and the coordinate axes. The mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1-x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/782b4df0220d84d90d26a4ad1fd4a34da00ecf3c5d62a9416d9f0490ca765e2b.png)\n\nFrom the description, the mass density function can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{y}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find an expression for $k$ in terms of $M$ by integrating the density function over the plate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}k{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}(1-x)^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{3}{[-\\frac{1}{4}(1-x)^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=12M$ and hence $\\lambda (x,y)=k{y}^{2}=12M{y}^{2}.$ Therefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{y}^{2}({y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{5}{y}^{5}]}_{0}^{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{5}(1-x)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{12M}{5}{[-\\frac{1}{6}(1-x)^{6}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{12M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-163186/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89f280af-9947-5d54-9284-9ae75d46c682"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163186"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163189/selection/7ca69d2ff12e034d894307e8fcddbe44ddaf9898c75007e6d8c20e393b3d4000" :answer/id #uuid "1a6dec5d-8904-5e76-b332-526199c33536" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7M}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163189/selection/50829d96b40881352b583e6c1c873c8aa6df59de6c7f79efbc380ec60ca9494e" :answer/id #uuid "2f79fbf5-ceb2-58cb-b025-5d89e2b58594" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163189/selection/697330ad097c7c0755610d42fbc780b7ae54890025eb09125ff7496222815e60" :answer/id #uuid "e9883c73-3b5e-5e84-a8d6-41d516bb16a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8M}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163189/selection/27701d4f36cee01c3a9deb6bf13199f617d617bcd02e48576f2d3fabde911537" :answer/id #uuid "02e6630c-651d-5a2c-b421-84ec3f775f36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163189/selection/b46df820bdeb989272f0bbb9084137cf2443a692578378dfe29e41bb10710705" :answer/id #uuid "69cf6182-90b0-56b9-8e61-b2bf21564f81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2M}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163189/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "55f4bfc2-50a7-54e6-af10-d51346698c9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163189/selection/697330ad097c7c0755610d42fbc780b7ae54890025eb09125ff7496222815e60" :answer-field/choices ["q-163189/selection/7ca69d2ff12e034d894307e8fcddbe44ddaf9898c75007e6d8c20e393b3d4000" "q-163189/selection/50829d96b40881352b583e6c1c873c8aa6df59de6c7f79efbc380ec60ca9494e" "q-163189/selection/697330ad097c7c0755610d42fbc780b7ae54890025eb09125ff7496222815e60" "q-163189/selection/27701d4f36cee01c3a9deb6bf13199f617d617bcd02e48576f2d3fabde911537" "q-163189/selection/b46df820bdeb989272f0bbb9084137cf2443a692578378dfe29e41bb10710705"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163189" :question/id #uuid "474a3fe6-26c2-5d5a-8503-ddb09ee16592" :question/math-academy-id "q-163189" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/37fde9d99a144ab65874a9fa329bc9a4ca32b0f4a6981993134e98c47a32e07f.png)\n\nA triangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant enclosed by the lines $y=x,$ $x=2,$ and the $x$-axis. The mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $y$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/f08ac68e3d8992e70cdc40eddfb9cdc39ee16a275890f3d9d7db42a682866bf6.png)\n\nFrom the description, the mass density function can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find an expression for $k$ in terms of $M$ by integrating the density function over the plate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}k{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[{x}^{2}y]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\frac{M}{4}$ and hence,\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2}=\\frac{M}{4}{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[{x}^{4}y]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{4}(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{[\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{6}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}\\cdot \\frac{32}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-163189/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89f280af-9947-5d54-9284-9ae75d46c682"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163189"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-162987"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/c290abf6acdff985b9c4aae6a998d7607b251a28285c9a8c15ff7c672e4ddc59.png)\n\nA triangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D$ in the first quadrant enclosed by the line $y=2-x$ and the coordinate axes. The mass density at each point is proportional to the sum of its distance from the $x$-axis and its distance from the $y$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2-x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/50ee44f265b3b27d7751e47a142053e06ee444b42481cd1277b5dacbb3ba8583.png)\n\nFrom the description, the mass density function can be written as \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k(|x|+|y|)=k(x+y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find an expression for $k$ in terms of $M$ by integrating the density function over the plate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}k(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}x+y\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[xy+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}x(2-x)+\\frac{1}{2}(2-x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}2-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{[2x-\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =k(4-\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8k}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\frac{3M}{8}$ and hence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k(x+y)=\\frac{3M}{8}(x+y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}{y}^{2}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}x{y}^{2}+{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}x{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=2-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}x(2-x)^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}(2-x)^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{12}(2-x)^{3}(x+6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{32}{\\int }_{0}^{2}-{x}^{4}+24{x}^{2}-64x+48\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{32}{[-\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}+8{x}^{3}-32{x}^{2}+48x]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{32}(-\\frac{32}{5}+64-128+96) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{32}\\cdot \\frac{128}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-162986"] :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $y$-axis.\nFind the moment of inertia of the lamina about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFrom the description, the mass density function can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find an expression for $k$ in terms of $M$ by integrating the density function over the plate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}k{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =k{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot [y]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =k(\\frac{1}{3}-0)(3-0) \\\\  & =k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=M$ and hence $\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2}=M{x}^{2}.$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =M{[\\frac{1}{5}y+\\frac{1}{9}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =M(\\frac{3}{5}+3-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{18M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-163242/selection/2d5cc1b82e4d2397aebab16900d6ac54fc2f42957cd22a51396b7f52816d146b" :answer/id #uuid "e7f21f84-2745-572f-818d-0cd8eb07553f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163242/selection/50829d96b40881352b583e6c1c873c8aa6df59de6c7f79efbc380ec60ca9494e" :answer/id #uuid "cd497303-f1f1-5811-9cae-4900033195e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163242/selection/167d2b11bf44b832a9ba8dc741d9cf2f1505f937a4dd5e96fc9d1759f78b6852" :answer/id #uuid "78e07db8-b668-530c-942c-fe79553c39e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{M}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163242/selection/c1cf1741ff3ce28c22251c4f3e2762a87f7716494a4c9965082e43b49bc9e431" :answer/id #uuid "6435fe47-e6d4-5682-945b-fa8cc369dfa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163242/selection/471e21b89b6b2b85430fa0dd260e07d2657e35b6fd5315405d72e9574319a0ec" :answer/id #uuid "7af9b035-fbd0-5066-9a00-8e00324ed2c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{M}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163242/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0d8985c-4b56-598b-8540-4e41803354e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163242/selection/50829d96b40881352b583e6c1c873c8aa6df59de6c7f79efbc380ec60ca9494e" :answer-field/choices ["q-163242/selection/2d5cc1b82e4d2397aebab16900d6ac54fc2f42957cd22a51396b7f52816d146b" "q-163242/selection/50829d96b40881352b583e6c1c873c8aa6df59de6c7f79efbc380ec60ca9494e" "q-163242/selection/167d2b11bf44b832a9ba8dc741d9cf2f1505f937a4dd5e96fc9d1759f78b6852" "q-163242/selection/c1cf1741ff3ce28c22251c4f3e2762a87f7716494a4c9965082e43b49bc9e431" "q-163242/selection/471e21b89b6b2b85430fa0dd260e07d2657e35b6fd5315405d72e9574319a0ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163242" :question/id #uuid "3def55ec-34fd-59d0-bba6-bc02cf16afcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-163242" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/d1a19303937f1d515ca820516e10a73974b00f83884b05abb58dee49c81207f4.png)\n\nConsider a plate of mass $M$ that occupies the region $D$ in the upper half plane bounded by the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16,$ shown above. Given that the mass is distributed uniformly across the plate, find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (r,\\theta ),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ in polar coordinates can be expressed as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 4,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe area of the plate $D$ is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2}=8\\pi .\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the mass is distributed uniformly, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{8\\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{8\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}{r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{8\\pi }({\\int }_{0}^{4}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{8\\pi }({\\int }_{0}^{4}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{8\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}{|}_{0}^{4}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\theta +\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{8\\pi }\\cdot 64\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =4M.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163242/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eba1f811-7b7d-56f6-8b49-4e7a4c7db81b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163242"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-38822/selection/f04c641aebfd02a59a39d16bd09bed61b27b8bea9f059402d9b8fe8c4b33ca94" :answer/id #uuid "3658ca36-08d0-5e0f-bafc-20ab62d9bb6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14M}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38822/selection/4985433892a53347dc012ea8f56a16136930edf6eda7fbddc313815388d19cca" :answer/id #uuid "39097f3b-e339-56c3-85ea-b1455eeb433e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16M}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38822/selection/27701d4f36cee01c3a9deb6bf13199f617d617bcd02e48576f2d3fabde911537" :answer/id #uuid "cc6a82bb-4c72-5958-80ae-6f77875da8a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38822/selection/2bd256f40fa75392b02ef5f029db8e05565ffa8fc87ad4b282e6428fab428c44" :answer/id #uuid "9bc6b333-2f93-5fb7-b376-4e22cd854b78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{28M}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38822/selection/56de7921a7a20e1e08bfb58d4fb65bb3153fed0d23aa43f0f5dd197e61a9602d" :answer/id #uuid "b90b5a0a-3df5-5d31-a16f-a7ebaa95c490" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21M}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38822/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e3a5a1e2-77d8-517c-8d3d-504629e93b24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-38822/selection/f04c641aebfd02a59a39d16bd09bed61b27b8bea9f059402d9b8fe8c4b33ca94" :answer-field/choices ["q-38822/selection/f04c641aebfd02a59a39d16bd09bed61b27b8bea9f059402d9b8fe8c4b33ca94" "q-38822/selection/4985433892a53347dc012ea8f56a16136930edf6eda7fbddc313815388d19cca" "q-38822/selection/27701d4f36cee01c3a9deb6bf13199f617d617bcd02e48576f2d3fabde911537" "q-38822/selection/2bd256f40fa75392b02ef5f029db8e05565ffa8fc87ad4b282e6428fab428c44" "q-38822/selection/56de7921a7a20e1e08bfb58d4fb65bb3153fed0d23aa43f0f5dd197e61a9602d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38822" :question/id #uuid "2eae4cf8-5a27-5bb2-bc3f-4dcf1775ac6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-38822" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/3b603e45dd1e5fe3073cad13a5577389736c1103840f3f904e29e738b4f2fd2e.png)\n\nConsider a plate of mass $M$ that occupies the region $D$ in the upper half plane bounded by the polar circles $r=1,$ $r=2,$ and the $x$-axis, as shown above. The mass density at any point is proportional to the square of its distance from the origin. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (r,\\theta ),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D,$ in polar coordinates, can be expressed as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nFrom the description, the mass density function can be written as $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=k{r}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find an expression for $k$ in terms of $M$ by integrating the density function over the plate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }k{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,\\text{d}r \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =k\\cdot \\frac{{r}^{4}}{4}{|}_{1}^{2}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =k\\cdot \\frac{15}{4}\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{15k\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=k{r}^{2}=\\frac{4M{r}^{2}}{15\\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{1}^{2}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}(64-1)\\cdot (\\pi -0) \\\\  & =\\frac{14M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-38822/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eba1f811-7b7d-56f6-8b49-4e7a4c7db81b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38822"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163228/selection/7073ddf865f0c9f97383f3a07b5458c92de9192b8b4e23bd69709c0792828aba" :answer/id #uuid "10549c83-7c09-5681-addb-db839d171f43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163228/selection/c2db034559420b121b995a068bdfea5fe16f2b700d9ebe187704e3ea55c1239e" :answer/id #uuid "6e6e0742-2720-5afe-811c-3dbf85e34cc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163228/selection/eb812f27219f6aa58813c9c74c442c8eeae741dad3c1dfa26acafe737dbee5f4" :answer/id #uuid "d5ac7b28-da9d-59db-9a14-f95a0e52500f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163228/selection/247b1021a5ebd7250d9146e3e81bce70ba7ecde69452157eff42be4985b42ca8" :answer/id #uuid "0235e39f-4899-563f-b750-9b6144eae62c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163228/selection/84aaba064027e7eb0bf329f6bc084c93277c0b932bcb0178f06baf24c9b9c48a" :answer/id #uuid "aba3ea2a-4d17-5950-95f9-b3cf3aa534e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163228/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "69501c94-9cc9-56b3-80cd-aa847b5d3a43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163228/selection/eb812f27219f6aa58813c9c74c442c8eeae741dad3c1dfa26acafe737dbee5f4" :answer-field/choices ["q-163228/selection/7073ddf865f0c9f97383f3a07b5458c92de9192b8b4e23bd69709c0792828aba" "q-163228/selection/c2db034559420b121b995a068bdfea5fe16f2b700d9ebe187704e3ea55c1239e" "q-163228/selection/eb812f27219f6aa58813c9c74c442c8eeae741dad3c1dfa26acafe737dbee5f4" "q-163228/selection/247b1021a5ebd7250d9146e3e81bce70ba7ecde69452157eff42be4985b42ca8" "q-163228/selection/84aaba064027e7eb0bf329f6bc084c93277c0b932bcb0178f06baf24c9b9c48a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163228" :question/id #uuid "5d537522-22cf-5837-a35b-5a4b7b536424" :question/math-academy-id "q-163228" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/044395de3b30755d0c83d489709c38420827f6984af740bc56a3dc5bfaa33794.png)\n\nConsider the plate that occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the polar circles $r=2$ and $r=3$ and the polar rays $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ in the first quadrant, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (r,\\theta ),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, note that the region $D$ in polar coordinates can be expressed as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,2\\le r\\le 3,\\,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nAlso, the mass density function in polar coordinates is \n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{1}{{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{2}^{3}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =({\\int }_{2}^{3}r\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{r}^{2}\\,{|}_{2}^{3}\\cdot \\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(9-4)\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163228/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eba1f811-7b7d-56f6-8b49-4e7a4c7db81b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163228"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163225/selection/1eff89b4e8e45dd246d56ebf6cfa52559748fd0647b109e09f1685f22aab8c16" :answer/id #uuid "148b67cd-5e6d-5122-8b85-df375fc39a1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "31\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163225/selection/f8f12b478d0323f303a6e66b7a5ba6a7f9a8c130ea62fc433a4fcbcf716a57c6" :answer/id #uuid "23e32cb4-858f-5260-ada4-11aef88bd8c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163225/selection/abe476e447976564bc5c670fe73789666287b967d49bbed12b1d85144449e63e" :answer/id #uuid "6ea984eb-8ee9-50ba-a64c-c051cb0ff9cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163225/selection/96ee6a3361e9d457b88fc124f1f022ef8dc27c2272728293b480cef1fc3f4e34" :answer/id #uuid "123883c4-49ea-51f6-8d86-af36715fefa9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163225/selection/42156604ab7e9ae5e57ff65983d38a3139c0e7e06b2396ddb0dde7f91f647ecd" :answer/id #uuid "1a18306e-b769-5961-943d-ed487a9c6ee5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163225/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1675b19d-6a25-51b5-b3d7-0c1339c6f8fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163225/selection/1eff89b4e8e45dd246d56ebf6cfa52559748fd0647b109e09f1685f22aab8c16" :answer-field/choices ["q-163225/selection/1eff89b4e8e45dd246d56ebf6cfa52559748fd0647b109e09f1685f22aab8c16" "q-163225/selection/f8f12b478d0323f303a6e66b7a5ba6a7f9a8c130ea62fc433a4fcbcf716a57c6" "q-163225/selection/abe476e447976564bc5c670fe73789666287b967d49bbed12b1d85144449e63e" "q-163225/selection/96ee6a3361e9d457b88fc124f1f022ef8dc27c2272728293b480cef1fc3f4e34" "q-163225/selection/42156604ab7e9ae5e57ff65983d38a3139c0e7e06b2396ddb0dde7f91f647ecd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163225" :question/id #uuid "92176aef-29a6-58f5-b012-4b4737ad5698" :question/math-academy-id "q-163225" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/d1ef5062d5bc045c1e1f7fa58c513315852f74aa15539c001662b0055583f01b.png)\n\nConsider the plate that occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the polar circles $r=1$ and $r=2$ and the polar rays $\\theta =0$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ in the first quadrant, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=10x.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (r,\\theta ),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, note that the region $D$ in polar coordinates can be expressed as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}}.\n$$\n\nAlso, the mass density function in polar coordinates is \n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=10r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}10r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}10{r}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{2}10{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =2{r}^{5}\\,{|}_{1}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =2(32-1)(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-0) \\\\  & =31\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-163225/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eba1f811-7b7d-56f6-8b49-4e7a4c7db81b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163225"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163243/selection/2d5cc1b82e4d2397aebab16900d6ac54fc2f42957cd22a51396b7f52816d146b" :answer/id #uuid "c06625e2-9b78-5546-8cb9-2d47c794a31a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163243/selection/a76e3ee4f865d6c2a9df0bd48d492bbb24f18ca0b45f19f823c1a6f6f867a586" :answer/id #uuid "079e4805-87e4-56ba-97bc-e281254d86b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3M}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163243/selection/c9067cd5c3287f49d8f514bcc0bd81695dfcd0cbc258703db0652d842d2af6a7" :answer/id #uuid "8b457ab8-6be3-5636-b5b7-87afeeffc0e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{M}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163243/selection/b85071a9e8b7d547fca77b2b77bca7f235cba5e00a1a199e5312d710423f08c1" :answer/id #uuid "798ddd70-aee5-5615-9921-f6a0fec105ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163243/selection/b46df820bdeb989272f0bbb9084137cf2443a692578378dfe29e41bb10710705" :answer/id #uuid "779f35a3-85fa-5fd1-be64-221cb452ca5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2M}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163243/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e895b614-920e-57d2-9e01-0f2d045a8adf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163243/selection/2d5cc1b82e4d2397aebab16900d6ac54fc2f42957cd22a51396b7f52816d146b" :answer-field/choices ["q-163243/selection/2d5cc1b82e4d2397aebab16900d6ac54fc2f42957cd22a51396b7f52816d146b" "q-163243/selection/a76e3ee4f865d6c2a9df0bd48d492bbb24f18ca0b45f19f823c1a6f6f867a586" "q-163243/selection/c9067cd5c3287f49d8f514bcc0bd81695dfcd0cbc258703db0652d842d2af6a7" "q-163243/selection/b85071a9e8b7d547fca77b2b77bca7f235cba5e00a1a199e5312d710423f08c1" "q-163243/selection/b46df820bdeb989272f0bbb9084137cf2443a692578378dfe29e41bb10710705"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163243" :question/id #uuid "fe5d4c58-2e38-5984-9eea-500802828713" :question/math-academy-id "q-163243" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/044386c438976bf17e2f51241659f167f7eedfb6509d0a60f3f70ba91457e71f.png)\n\nConsider a plate of mass $M$ that occupies the region $D$ in the first, second and third quadrants bounded by the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4,$ shown above. Given that the mass is distributed uniformly across the plate, find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (r,\\theta ),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ in polar coordinates can be expressed as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe area of the plate $D$ is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{3}{4}\\pi {r}^{2}=3\\pi .\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the mass is distributed uniformly, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{3\\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3\\pi }({\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3\\pi }({\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}{|}_{0}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\theta -\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ){|}_{0}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3\\pi }\\cdot 4\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =M.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163243/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eba1f811-7b7d-56f6-8b49-4e7a4c7db81b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163243"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8543"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/46d6a57700d1df7f2de9a46507821a8553876eb956be6ef87a455d5ca0fabafb.png)\n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the curves $y=x^2$ and $y=1$ in the first quadrant, as shown above. If the mass density function of $D$ is given by $\\lambda(x,y) = 4xy,$ find the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda(x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nI_x =  \\iint\\limits_D y^2\\lambda(x,y)  \\:\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nI_y =  \\iint\\limits_D x^2\\lambda(x,y)  \\:\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\nI_0 = \\iint\\limits_D (x^2+y^2) \\lambda(x,y)  \\:\\textrm{d}A = I_x + I_y.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: x^2 \\leq y \\leq 1 \\right\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/8846da0fe3b1e8369a9277bbaba1e082d040136a71105a5816af7b13d2788027.png)\n\nUsing the formula for $I_x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}{y}^{2}\\cdot 4xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}4x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[x{y}^{4}]_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(1-{x}^{8})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x-{x}^{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{10}}{10}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8542"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/de882e240d0a6ca824e77397fe9c6b51eb94d36c2e5e3524422ef0a0f28103de.png)\n\nA triangular plate of mass ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/48c72d7f57bb7f3163fa37903a032773c12ddce6fdc0e0bee8818259aba9e465.png) and uniform mass density occupies the region ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/05ff793b0aee1f05a79216f9e7f119afa544749c81077937f8f06a353f6ef4eb.png) enclosed between the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/54d73239bada862f9b8d6d3d7a4f73bea15432668f6b2116098faa02a4b3d435.png)-axis and the lines ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/3879c9475dcb86235e269108d73767f2e631eee68e65aacbfffbc22ada2033e1.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/52ab6e6677e9404e8b08bfff7b90cbfb332b344d4fe8ecc19b603ef05616ebf7.png) as shown above. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/f0a3d06d2c55c6889a22a1cc4e11adb35b71e24e1395e6d6048c1135620c225f.png)-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069995/assets/28390f00cdb34a228868c36035ff66f1ea65bf7ff5e592fa473fca18d6addbcc.png) with mass density function ![](/home